Fixed BLE name DIY-2_13-6429 (no letter): the old-HM 2_13 family speaks our protocol.

Three device lines share the 2.13" size but speak different BLE services:
  DIY-2_13-xxxx  old v1.10, HMCLOCK lineage, 16-bit 0xFF00 (family_hm)
  DIY-2_13N-xxxx new-gen B/W, 128-bit 6275 vendor service (2_13n family)
  DIY-2_13C-xxxx color, 128-bit 6275 vendor service (2_13c family)
This firmware implements FF00/FF01 only, so only the no-letter name routes
to a webtool family that can talk to it. N or C would connect the picker
to a family demanding the 6275 service we do not expose.

Suffix 6429 is hardcoded, not OTP-derived: HMCLOCK's OTP transform may
produce a different suffix than the vendor firmware on this tag. Fixed name
keeps picker filter + family routing stable across every future image.
Single-tag assumption: two tags with this build would advertise identically.
Applied to the build copy only.

--- a/src/user_peripheral.c
+++ b/src/user_peripheral.c
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
 static int otp_btaddr[2];                      // Bluetooth address read from OTP
 static int otp_boot;                           // Boot-related data read from OTP
 static char adv_name[20];                      // Advertised name buffer
-char *bt_id = adv_name+7;                      // Start of the Bluetooth ID within the advertised name (right after "DCLK-")
+char *bt_id = adv_name+11;                     // Start of the Bluetooth ID within the advertised name (right after "DIY-2_13-")
 int clock_interval;                            // Clock update interval (seconds)
 int clock_fixup_value;                         // Clock drift correction value
 int clock_fixup_count;                         // Clock drift correction counter
@@ -151,10 +151,12 @@
 	ba0 &= 0x00ffffff;
 	ba0 ^= ba1;
 
-	// Build the advertised name (format: DCLK-XXYYZZ, where XXYYZZ are the last
-	// three bytes of the Bluetooth address)
-	u8 *ba = (u8*)&ba0;
-	sprintf(adv_name+2, "DCLK-%02x%02x%02x", ba[2], ba[1], ba[0]);
+	// Fixed advertised name: byte-identical to the vendor firmware on this tag.
+	// (HMCLOCK derives the suffix from OTP with its own transform; the vendor
+	// suffix 6429 may differ. A fixed name keeps picker filter + family routing
+	// stable across every future image.)
+	memcpy(adv_name+2, "DIY-2_13-6429", 13);
+	(void)ba0; (void)ba1;
 	int name_len = strlen(adv_name+2);
 
 	// If the device name hasn't been set, use the generated name
